          "kicker": "Tribute weekend",
          "heading": "FFR orders minute’s applause before all French rugby matches for Cléa Menier",
          "body": "French rugby will pay tribute this weekend to 17-year-old Cléa Menier, who died in hospital in Bordeaux after an on-field injury during an under-18 match for Union du Bassin Marmandais against Agen Agglo Rugby. The French Rugby Federation says a minute’s applause will be held before each professional and amateur match in France this weekend, and that French rugby is “deeply shaken” by her death. Her club called it “an accident”; neither the club nor the FFR has disclosed the nature of the injury."
