          "heading": "Scarlets' Macs Page forced off wearing oxygen mask after a head knock",
          "body": "Scarlets wing Macs Page, the uncapped 21-year-old who narrowly missed Steve Tandy's autumn squad, was forced off in their United Rugby Championship match against the Stormers in Cape Town. His head hit the turf as he tried to score, and after a stretcher was brought on he walked off receiving oxygen, with medics holding his head. Page had already crossed for his fifth try of the season, and Scarlets director of rugby Nigel Davies said it was only a matter of time before Wales called him up."
